# Web app build settings (Vite reads them from the environment or from apps/web/.env*).
# Values are compiled into the bundle, so never put a secret here.

# The API's root URL, including its /api prefix: a path on the web app's own origin, or an
# absolute URL when the API is served from another origin (that origin must then be listed in
# the API's CORS_ORIGINS). A trailing slash is ignored. Any other value (`api`, or an absolute
# URL without a path) stops `vite build` and `vite` with an error.
# Unset: /api on the web app's origin. `npm run dev` and `vite preview` forward /api to the
# local API (port 3001, or API_PORT; API_PROXY_TARGET, read from the shell, points them at an
# API elsewhere); the web image is built with /api and nginx forwards it.
# VITE_API_URL=https://api.example.com/api

# Where the footer's "Source" link points: the source code of the version you deploy, so a
# modified version served to others links to its own source. An http(s) address; unset, empty
# or anything else links to https://github.com/josefdc/liner-notes.
# VITE_SOURCE_URL=https://github.com/you/liner-notes

# The Cloudflare Turnstile site key (public) for the widget shown before an analysis starts.
# Leave it unset for now: this version has no Turnstile widget yet, so a build with a site key
# cannot verify any request and says so instead of starting an analysis. Set it once the widget
# ships.
# Unset: the app asks the API for a run token with the development answer, which only an API
# in development (NODE_ENV=development or test) without a Turnstile secret accepts.
# VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=
